@beihaizb/dsh-notebook README · Features (implemented)：- **Real persistent kernel**: `ipykernel` + `jupyter_client` sidecar — variables persist across cells. **R kernels** (`IRkernel`) are supported too, picked from the same dropdown.
- **Agent tools** to read, edit, run, and inspect cells (`nb_get`, `nb_edit_cell`, `nb_run_cell`, ...) with structured access to outputs and tracebacks.
- **Runtime introspection for agents (safety-first)**: `nb_context`, `nb_list_vars`, and `nb_inspect_object` expose live kernel variables and compact notebook state, but **never call `repr()` on an arbitrary object**. `nb_list_vars` returns name, exact type, and shape only, with `pattern` filtering and `offset`/`limit` paging (default 100, max 200, `max_chars` bounds the payload); `nb_inspect_object` returns type/shape by default and only a bounded preview when `preview=true` is passed **and** the object is an allowlisted exact type (builtin containers and scalars, NumPy arrays, pandas `DataFrame`/`Series`, scipy sparse matrices, `AnnData` shape/`isbacked`). Unknown types stay metadata-only. With no kernel running it answers `not_started` (**it will not start one just to look at variables**); while a

@beihaizb/dsh-notebook README · Introspection contract：```text
nb_list_vars({ pattern?, offset?, limit?, max_chars? })
  -> { status, source, kernel_state, vars:[{name,type,module?,shape?}],
       total, offset, next_offset, truncated }

@beihaizb/dsh-notebook README · Introspection contract：- `status` is `ok` / `busy` / `not_started` / `timeout` / `error`. `busy` and `not_started` are answers, not failures: retry at another moment instead of starting a kernel.
- `name` is a **literal**, never an expression — `__import__('os')` yields `found: false`.
- No variable contents are returned unless `preview: true`, and even then only for allowlisted exact types, bounded to 20 rows / 50 columns and a `max_chars` budget (1024–64000).
